{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/jobsvalkey"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"topicSections":[{"title":"Job Queue","anchor":"Job-Queue","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.opticalaberration.hummingbird\/documentation\/JobsValkey\/ValkeyJobQueue"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Structures","anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.opticalaberration.hummingbird\/documentation\/JobsValkey\/ValkeyJobCleanupParameters","doc:\/\/com.opticalaberration.hummingbird\/documentation\/JobsValkey\/ValkeyOrphanedJobCleanupParameters"]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"JobsValkey","images":[{"type":"icon","identifier":"logo.png"}],"title":"JobsValkey","symbolKind":"module","role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"JobsValkey"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Jobs Queue driver using "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/valkey-io\/valkey-swift"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Setup","anchor":"Setup"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Valkey job queue driver uses "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ValkeyClient"},{"type":"text","text":" from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"valkey-swift"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The Valkey job queue configuration includes three values.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"pollTime","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": This is the amount of time between the last time the queue was empty and the next time the driver starts looking for pending jobs.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"queueName","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": Name of queue used to differentiate itself from other queues.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"retentionPolicy"},{"type":"text","text":": Policy on what jobs are retained."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import JobsValkey","import ServiceLifecycle","import Valkey","","let valkeyClient = ValkeyClient(...)","let jobService = JobService(","    .valkey(","        valkeyClient,","        configuration: .init(","            queueName: \"MyJobQueue\",","            pollTime: .milliseconds(50)","        )","    ), ","    logger: logger",")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Additional Features","anchor":"Additional-Features"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"There are features specific to the Valkey\/Redis Job Queue implementation.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Push Options","anchor":"Push-Options"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When pushing a job to the queue there are a number of options you can provide.","type":"text"}]},{"level":4,"type":"heading","text":"Delaying jobs","anchor":"Delaying-jobs"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"As with all queue drivers you can add a delay before a job is processed. The job will sit in the pending queue and will not be available for processing until time has passed its delay until time.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Add TestJob to the queue, but don't process it for 2 minutes","try await jobService.push(TestJob(), options: .init(delayUntil: .now + 120))"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Cancellation","anchor":"Cancellation"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.opticalaberration.hummingbird\/documentation\/JobsValkey\/ValkeyJobQueue","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" conforms to protocol ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.opticalaberration.hummingbird\/documentation\/Jobs\/CancellableJobQueue","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". This requires support for cancelling jobs that are in the pending queue. It adds one new function ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.opticalaberration.hummingbird\/documentation\/JobsValkey\/ValkeyJobQueue\/cancel(jobID:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". If you supply this function with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"JobID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" returned by ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.opticalaberration.hummingbird\/documentation\/JobsValkey\/ValkeyJobQueue\/push(_:options:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" it will remove it from the pending queue.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Add TestJob to the queue and immediately cancel it","let jobID = try await jobService.push(TestJob(), options: .init(delayUntil: .now + 120))","try await jobService.cancel(jobID: jobID)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Pause and Resume","anchor":"Pause-and-Resume"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.opticalaberration.hummingbird\/documentation\/JobsValkey\/ValkeyJobQueue"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to protocol "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.opticalaberration.hummingbird\/documentation\/Jobs\/ResumableJobQueue"},{"type":"text","text":". This requires support for pausing and resuming jobs that are in the pending queue. It adds two new functions "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.opticalaberration.hummingbird\/documentation\/JobsValkey\/ValkeyJobQueue\/pause(jobID:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.opticalaberration.hummingbird\/documentation\/JobsValkey\/ValkeyJobQueue\/resume(jobID:)"},{"type":"text","text":". If you supply these function with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"JobID"},{"type":"text","text":" returned by "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.opticalaberration.hummingbird\/documentation\/JobsValkey\/ValkeyJobQueue\/push(_:options:)"},{"type":"text","text":" you can remove from the pending queue and add them back in at a later date."}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Add TestJob to the queue and immediately remove it and then add it back to the queue","let jobID = try await jobService.push(TestJob(), options: .init(delayUntil: .now + 120))","try await jobService.pause(jobID: jobID)","try await jobService.resume(jobID: jobID)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Job retention","anchor":"Job-retention"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The queue has options to retain jobs once it has finished with them depending on status. By default the queue will retain failed jobs and drop cancelled or completed jobs, but these decisions are configurable.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let jobService = JobService(","    .valkey(","        valkeyClient, ","        configuration: .init(","            queueKey: \"MyJobQueue\", ","            retentionPolicy: .init(","                completedJobs: .retain, ","                failedJobs: .retain, ","                cancelledJobs: .doNotRetain","            )","        )","    ),","    logger: logger",")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Job queue cleanup","anchor":"Job-queue-cleanup"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you do opt to retain jobs after processing you will probably eventually want to clean them up. The Valkey\/Redis queue provides a method ","type":"text"},{"code":"cleanup","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" which allows you to remove or attempt to re-run jobs based on what state they are in. You should be careful not to do anything to pending or processing jobs while the job queue is being processed as it might confuse the job processor.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["jobService.queue.queue.cleanup(","    pendingJobs: .doNothing,","    processingJobs: .doNothing,","    completedJobs: .remove(maxAge: .seconds(7*24*60*60)),","    failedJobs: .rerun,","    cancelledJobs: .remove, ","    pausedJobs: .doNothing",")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":4,"type":"heading","text":"Scheduling cleanup","anchor":"Scheduling-cleanup"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Given this is a job you will probably want to do regularly the queue also provides a job you can use in conjunction with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"JobScheduler","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that will do the cleanup for you. There are options to set this up at initialization of your ","type":"text"},{"code":"JobService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let jobService = JobService(","    .valkey(...),","    logger: logger,","    options: .init(","        cleanup: .init(","            jobs: .init(","                parameters: .init(completedJobs: .remove(maxAge: .seconds(60*60*24*7))),","                schedule: .weekly(day: .sunday)","            )","        )","    )",")"],"type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.opticalaberration.hummingbird\/documentation\/Jobs","doc:\/\/com.opticalaberration.hummingbird\/documentation\/JobsPostgres","doc:\/\/com.opticalaberration.hummingbird\/documentation\/Hummingbird"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Reference","anchor":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.opticalaberration.hummingbird\/documentation\/JobsPostgres"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Valkey\/Redis implementation for swift-jobs framework"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.opticalaberration.hummingbird\/documentation\/JobsValkey","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"https://github.com/valkey-io/valkey-swift":{"titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"valkey-swift"}],"identifier":"https:\/\/github.